-		<English>[H1]Route (Railroad)[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Roads and railroads allow units to move longer distances within a turn by reducing the movement costs of terrain.[PARAGRAPH:1]When a unit is within hostile cultural borders, roads and railroads have no effect unless the unit has the Commando promotion. When the civilization has an Open Borders agreement allowing their units right of passage, they may freely take advantage of roads and railroads.[PARAGRAPH:2]To build railroads, the civilization first needs to discover the Railroad technology and have an access to Coal or Oil. Railroads are similar to roads, but they reduce the number of [ICON_MOVES] Movement points needed to enter a tile from another railroad tile to 1/10 [ICON_MOVES] MP.[PARAGRAPH:1]Railroads also give a bonus of 1 [ICON_PRODUCTION] to tiles with a [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_MINE]Mine[\LINK], a [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_LUMBERMILL]Lumbermill[\LINK], or a [LINK=IMPROVEMENT_QUARRY]Quarry[\LINK].[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Source: https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/Road_and_railroad_(Civ4)</English>
